    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0261" n="179" xml:id="pg179"/>

                <head>Mr. Wood to Mr. Hunter</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No 197.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Copenhagen,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 6, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I herewith enclose a copy of my note to Mr.
                    Blumhe, minister for foreign affairs, on transmitting him the President’s
                    proclamation of the 10th of May, ultimo, in relation to the national ships of
                    other powers. By reference to my despatch No. 193, you will see that that
                    proclamation is not applicable to this government.</p>
                <p>I remain, &amp;c., your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>BRADFORD R. WOOD, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident,
                            &amp;c.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Hunter,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d184-a1.xml" xpointer="d184-a1"/>
